f <MATH_0009> to the object <MATH_0010>\nof <MATH_0011> over <MATH_0012>, see proof of\nQuot, Proposition <REF_0001>. Hence we can form\nthe fibre product diagram\n<MATH_0013>\nThis is the defining diagram for the algebraic space in the\nupper left corner. The left vertical arrow is a\nflat closed immersion which is an open and closed immersion\nfor example if <MATH_0014> is finite, or <MATH_0015> is locally Noetherian, or\n<MATH_0016> and <MATH_0017> for some\ninvertible <MATH_0018>-module <MATH_0019> (in the last\ncase we sometimes use the notation\n<MATH_0020>).\nSee Situation <REF_0002> and\nLemmas <REF_0003> and <REF_0004> and\nExample <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:33e75ac3e582cb810aad71e34ec2e663503809cf161b28f3c235bebc3cc1ae8a", "unit_id": "tag:0DP6:statement"}
